# tree288_100Gbps.topo — scale-out tier for the G72 application suite.
#
# Structural scale-up of pcm's example tree16.topo (same 100 Gbps host links,
# same 2-tier oversubscribed shape, same latencies): the pcm federation gives
# EVERY GPU its own scale-out NIC (rank = scale-out endpoint), so the
# scale-out topology must hold >= total ranks. tree16 caps the suite at 16
# ranks — the G72 configs need up to 288 (72 x 2 x 2). 288 hosts as 12 ToRs
# x 24 hosts, 2:1 oversubscribed (Radix_Up 12): 12 aggs, each ToR linked once
# to each agg (parser invariant: n_agg = tor_uplinks / T1_radix_down must
# equal ToR Radix_Up => T1 Radix_Down = #ToRs = 12).
Nodes 288
Tiers 2
Podsize 288

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
Radix_Down 24
Radix_Up 12
Downlink_Latency_ns 1
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Oversubscribed 2

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 100
Radix_Down 12
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
